{"id":"mahabharata-11-019","work":"mahabharata","part":11,"partName":"स्त्रीपर्व","partNameEn":"Stri Parva","unit":19,"title":"एकोनविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 19 · Vikarna and Duryodhana's family","summary":{"en":"Gandhari shows Krishna her son Vikarna, whose face is half-eaten by beasts, and Duryodhana's wife and mother beside their dead lords. She names the princes and tells of the fallen kings.","kn":"ಗಾಂಧಾರಿ ಮೃಗಗಳು ಅರ್ಧ ತಿಂದ ಮುಖದ ಮಗ ವಿಕರ್ಣನನ್ನು, ಹತರಾದ ಪತಿಗಳ ಬಳಿ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಪತ್ನಿ, ತಾಯಿಯನ್ನು ಕೃಷ್ಣನಿಗೆ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ರಾಜಕುಮಾರರನ್ನು ಹೆಸರಿಸಿ ಬಿದ್ದ ರಾಜರ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"गान्धारी कृष्ण को अपने पुत्र विकर्ण को दिखाती हैं जिसका मुख पशुओं ने आधा खा लिया है, और मृत पतियों के पास दुर्योधन की पत्नी तथा माता को। वे राजकुमारों के नाम लेकर गिरे राजाओं की बात करती हैं।","te":"గాంధారి మృగాలు సగం తిన్న ముఖంతో ఉన్న కొడుకు వికర్ణుని, మరణించిన భర్తల పక్కన దుర్యోధనుని భార్యను, తల్లిని కృష్ణునికి చూపుతుంది. రాకుమారుల పేర్లు చెప్పి పడిన రాజుల గురించి చెబుతుంది.","ta":"காந்தாரி விலங்குகள் பாதி தின்ற முகத்துடன் உள்ள மகன் விகர்ணனையும் இறந்த கணவரருகே துரியோதனனின் மனைவியையும் தாயையும் கண்ணனுக்குக் காட்டுகிறாள். இளவரசர்களைப் பெயரிட்டு வீழ்ந்த மன்னர்களைப் பற்றிக் கூறுகிறாள்.","ml":"തന്റെ പുത്രൻ വികർണ്ണന്റെ മുഖം പകുതി മൃഗങ്ങൾ തിന്നുതീർത്ത നിലയിൽ ഗാന്ധാരി കൃഷ്ണനെ കാണിക്കുന്നു; മരിച്ച ഭർത്താക്കന്മാർക്കരികിൽ ദുര്യോധനന്റെ ഭാര്യയും അമ്മയും ഇരിക്കുന്നു. രാജകുമാരന്മാരുടെ പേരുകൾ പറയുകയും വീണ രാജാക്കന്മാരെക്കുറിച്ച് അവൾ പറയുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 11.19; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 17 2017","sections":[{"title":"स्त्रीविलापपर्व","titleEn":"Strivilapa Parva (Lament of the women)","verses":[{"text":"गान्धार्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Gandhari said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एष माधव पुत्रो मे विकर्णः प्राज्ञसंमतः ।\nभूमौ विनिहतः शेते भीमेन शतधा कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhava, here is my son Vikarna, whom the wise respected, lying struck down on the ground, cut apart by Bhima."}},{"n":2,"text":"गजमध्यगतः शेते विकर्णो मधुसूदन ।\nनीलमेघपरिक्षिप्तः शरदीव दिवाकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, Vikarna lies in the midst of elephants, like the sun in autumn ringed by dark clouds."}},{"n":3,"text":"अस्य चापग्रहेणैष पाणिः कृतकिणो महान् ।\nकथंचिच्छिद्यते गृध्रैरत्तुकामैस्तलत्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great hand of this one, calloused by the bowstring and wearing its glove, is being torn by vultures who want to eat it."}},{"n":4,"text":"अस्य भार्यामिषप्रेप्सून्गृध्रानेतांस्तपस्विनी ।\nवारयत्यनिशं बाला न च शक्नोति माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"His young wife, the poor woman, keeps driving away the vultures that crave flesh, but she cannot, Madhava."}},{"n":5,"text":"युवा वृन्दारकः शूरो विकर्णः पुरुषर्षभ ।\nसुखोचितः सुखार्हश्च शेते पांसुषु माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhava, bull among men, the young, splendid hero Vikarna, used to comfort and worthy of comfort, lies in the dust."}},{"n":6,"text":"कर्णिनालीकनाराचैर्भिन्नमर्माणमाहवे ।\nअद्यापि न जहात्येनं लक्ष्मीर्भरतसत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His vital parts were pierced in battle by arrows, long and short, but even now glory does not leave this best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":7,"text":"एष संग्रामशूरेण प्रतिज्ञां पालयिष्यता ।\nदुर्मुखोऽभिमुखः शेते हतोऽरिगणहा रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here lies Durmukha, slayer of enemy hosts, struck in battle facing the foe, keeping the vow of a hero in battle."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्यैतद्वदनं कृष्ण श्वापदैरर्धभक्षितम् ।\nविभात्यभ्यधिकं तात सप्तम्यामिव चन्द्रमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, his face, half eaten by beasts, shines all the more, dear one, like the moon on the seventh day."}},{"n":9,"text":"शूरस्य हि रणे कृष्ण यस्याननमथेदृशम् ।\nस कथं निहतोऽमित्रैः पांसून्ग्रसति मे सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna, how does my son, the hero in battle whose face is like this, lie slain by enemies, eating the dust?"}},{"n":10,"text":"यस्याहवमुखे सौम्य स्थाता नैवोपपद्यते ।\nस कथं दुर्मुखोऽमित्रैर्हतो विबुधलोकजित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How has Durmukha, who conquered the world of the gods, been killed by his enemies, he before whom no one could stand at the head of battle, gentle one?"}},{"n":11,"text":"चित्रसेनं हतं भूमौ शयानं मधुसूदन ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रमिमं पश्य प्रतिमानं दनुष्मताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, look at Chitrasena, slain and lying on the ground, this son of Dhritarashtra, equal to the greatest archers."}},{"n":12,"text":"तं चित्रमाल्याभरणं युवत्यः शोककर्शिताः ।\nक्रव्यादसंघैः सहिता रुदन्त्यः पर्युपासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Young women wasted with grief, weeping, sit with flocks of flesh-eaters around him, who wore bright garlands and ornaments."}},{"n":13,"text":"स्त्रीणां रुदितनिर्घोषः श्वापदानां च गर्जितम् ।\nचित्ररूपमिदं कृष्ण विचित्रं प्रतिभाति मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The weeping cries of the women and the roars of the beasts together seem to me strange and various, Krishna."}},{"n":14,"text":"युवा वृन्दारको नित्यं प्रवरस्त्रीनिषेवितः ।\nविविंशतिरसौ शेते ध्वस्तः पांसुषु माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here lies Vivimshati, ever young and splendid, attended by the best of women, destroyed in the dust, Madhava."}},{"n":15,"text":"शरसंकृत्तवर्माणं वीरं विशसने हतम् ।\nपरिवार्यासते गृध्राः परिविंशा विविंशतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vultures surround the hero Vivimshati, killed in the slaughter, his armor cut by arrows, as if they were his kin."}},{"n":16,"text":"प्रविश्य समरे वीरः पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ।\nआविश्य शयने शेते पुनः सत्पुरुषोचितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering the Pandava army in battle, the hero lies on the bed as is fit for a good man."}},{"n":17,"text":"स्मितोपपन्नं सुनसं सुभ्रु ताराधिपोपमम् ।\nअतीव शुभ्रं वदनं पश्य कृष्ण विविंशतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Krishna, at Vivimshati's face, still with a smile, fine-nosed, fine-browed, like the lord of stars, exceedingly bright."}},{"n":18,"text":"यं स्म तं पर्युपासन्ते वसुं वासवयोषितः ।\nक्रीडन्तमिव गन्धर्वं देवकन्याः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He whom the women of Indra attended, like the Vasu, as if he were a gandharva at play, with thousands of divine maidens,"}},{"n":19,"text":"हन्तारं वीरसेनानां शूरं समितिशोभनम् ।\nनिबर्हणममित्राणां दुःसहं विषहेत कः ॥","meaning":{"en":"slayer of the heroes' armies, brave, glorious in assemblies, destroyer of foes: who could withstand that hard-to-bear one?"}},{"n":20,"text":"दुःसहस्यैतदाभाति शरीरं संवृतं शरैः ।\nगिरिरात्मरुहैः फुल्लैः कर्णिकारैरिवावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The body of Duhsaha, pierced by arrows, shines like a mountain covered with flowering karnikara trees that have grown on it."}},{"n":21,"text":"शातकौम्भ्या स्रजा भाति कवचेन च भास्वता ।\nअग्निनेव गिरिः श्वेतो गतासुरपि दुःसहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his golden garland and shining armor, even lifeless he is hard to bear, shining like a white mountain with fire upon it."}}]}]}